  "quotation": "const getTargetMutagens = (heavenlyStem: HeavenlyStemKey) => {\n  const { mutagens } = getConfig();\n  let result;\n\n  if (mutagens && mutagens[heavenlyStem]) {\n    result = mutagens[heavenlyStem] ?? [];\n  } else {\n    result = heavenlyStems[heavenlyStem].mutagen ?? [];\n  }\n\n  return result;\n};",
  "conditionAnalysis": [
    "The combined base branch and stem arithmetic matches getHoroscope: twelve ten-year ranges start at Cục; direction follows sex and birth branch polarity; the physical Dần-relative palace index, added to TIGER_RULE of the trusted lunar birth stem modulo ten, supplies the selected decadal stem. T025/T030 acceptance remains a prerequisite, and cannot approve this extension by inheritance.",
    "FunctionalAstrolabe selects an inclusive actual decadal range and calls getMutagensByHeavenlyStem with that period heavenlyStem. decadalList confirms the same connection. The new explicit profile must not substitute natal or viewed-year stem, or adopt upstream childhood fallback/date-derived age.",
    "The ten four-entry rows match the complete pinned built-in table, including Mậu Khoa Hữu Bật and Nhâm Khoa Tả Phù. MUTAGEN order is Lộc, Quyền, Khoa, Kỵ. Hóa-prefixed labels and output IDs are declared B3 presentation mapping. Runtime reuse of the natal table requires strict full-content equality with the immutable approved snapshot and does not authenticate natal formulas.",
    "getTargetMutagens prefers a configured row; even an empty array overrides the default. resolveConfig accepts arbitrary lengths, and bindContext retains creation-time config/language. The fixed-table projection therefore excludes arbitrary/global/context overrides and cannot claim a later reset makes existing source objects default.",
    "hasHoroscopeMutagen resolves a scope-relative role to physical index, then tests natal majorStars plus minorStars against the ordered scope mutagen target. It inserts no transformation stars. The proposed inverse associations preserve existing physical natal palace and function identity; they do not rotate decadal roles or implement the source boolean query API.",
    "All fifteen canonical source targets and adapter IDs/classifications agree with the parsed Vietnamese source and replayed B3 metadata. Eleven principal targets are major/chinh_tinh; the four auxiliaries use good/phu_tinh. These are B3 adapter classifications and existing physical locations, not independent proof of upstream or B3 natal placement formulas.",
    "Exactly-one coherent selected-target occurrence is a stricter product integrity guard, not an upstream uniqueness theorem. A malformed duplicate could satisfy source membership at multiple palaces. Missing/duplicate/conflicting metadata must close the whole combined output, including selected stem/branch. Legitimate different stars sharing one palace retain four ordered records.",
    "The replay covers all ten selected stems and fifteen source targets, both sexes/directions and Cục 2–6, and distinguishes natal/year substitution, offset and category-order errors. It demonstrates candidate arithmetic and existing T030 behavior; the new runtime adapter and its synthetic malformed-input guards remain to be implemented and tested.",
    "Classical generic activation, existing natal/default/source promotion, outcome interpretation and public/production release remain outside this judgment. No additional source-semantic prerequisite beyond the declared conditions was found for this narrow projection."
  ],
